1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:08,050
Your credit card bill arrives at ten million dong, and tapping the five-hundred-thousand-dong minimum counts as paying on time with zero late penalty.

2
00:00:08,050 --> 00:00:11,850
So why does next month's debt jump above ten million ninety-two thousand?

3
00:00:12,690 --> 00:00:18,060
Because two business days after your swipe, your card issuer already wired real cash to pay the store.

4
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:23,370
Those forty-five interest-free days stay intact only when you settle one hundred percent of the bill.

5
00:00:24,090 --> 00:00:33,370
Pay only five hundred thousand on day forty-five and you dodge late penalties and overdue credit marks, yet every single one of those forty-five free days vanishes right away.

6
00:00:34,330 --> 00:00:47,810
At an illustrative zero point one percent per day, the bank charges four hundred and fifty thousand for forty-five days on ten million, plus one hundred and forty-two thousand five hundred on nine point five million.

7
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:58,170
Both slices add up to five hundred and ninety-two thousand five hundred dong — beating your five-hundred-thousand payout and pushing your bill to ten million ninety-two thousand five hundred.

8
00:00:59,060 --> 00:01:02,710
Save that minimum button for genuine cash crunches.

9
00:01:02,710 --> 00:01:09,730
Whenever checking holds the cash, settle one hundred percent on time to keep forty-five days free.
